# Agent ops (hermes-stack)

Follow **[docs/AGENT_RULES.md](../../docs/AGENT_RULES.md)** as the editable source of truth (role + numbered rules). Git details: **[docs/GIT.md](../../docs/GIT.md)**.

## Hard gates (every turn)

- **No lab identity in product source:** no VPS IPs, SSH users, passwords, or API keys in committed `scripts/`, `test/`, or docs. Host probes go in gitignored `scripts/temp/` / `hermes/temp/`.
- Switch to **`develop`**, then `feature/*`, before new work.
- **No** VPS deploy / remote test scripts without explicit permission.
- **No** push or MR without explicit permission.
- After a test run finishes, **restore product defaults** (no leftover lab-only config).
- Update **`docs/CHANGELOG.md`** (top entry + timestamp) for product/ops changes.
- Prefer **skills + editable config/messages** over hardcoded keywords or chat strings.
- SSH/remote bash: **LF only**, prefer single-line SSH, fail on non-zero exit.
- Features must be **enable/disable components**; reuse Valkey/queues/etc. instead of inventing caches.
- Knowledge cite/list: **top 5** + count of the rest.

## Remote sync helper

When the operator allows remote update, prefer:

`pwsh -File scripts/main/Update-StackRemote.ps1 ...`

(Do not invent one-off Paramiko/SSH test payloads without permission.)
